\section{Levels}{

Every message has a level. The levels are given by the \code{OL} object, a list
whose components are, in ascending order of priority, \code{Debug}, \code{Verbose},
\code{Info}, \code{Warning}, \code{Question}, \code{Error} and \code{Fatal}. Messages at level \code{Error}
or \code{Fatal} stop execution. There is also an \code{Ignore} level, below \code{Debug},
which is used with \code{\link[=reportAs]{reportAs()}} to suppress a class of message entirely.

Wherever reportr expects a level, it may be given as \code{OL$Info}, as the bare
name \code{Info}, or as the string \code{"Info"}.
}

