\item \code{reportrTimeFormat}: The format used for the time in prefixes, as
understood by \code{\link[=format.POSIXct]{format.POSIXct()}}. The default is \code{"\%Y-\%m-\%d \%H:\%M:\%S"}.
\item \code{reportrStderrLevel}: The level at and above which the terminal writes
messages to standard error rather than standard output, unless the
terminal target specifies its own. The default is \code{Warning}.
\item \code{reportrStackTraceLevel}: The level at and above which a stack trace is
written with each message, when the output level is \code{Debug}. The default
